.TH KAST 1 "2026-07-26" "kast 0.8.0" "kast manual"
.SH NAME
kast \- Win+K-style cast panel for GNOME
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kast
.RI [ verb ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kast
wires AirPlay, Chromecast and Miracast into one GNOME Quick Settings tile, one
.B Super+K
shortcut, and one CLI. With no verb, it runs
.BR status .
Almost every verb that prints something accepts
.BR \-\-json ,
which is how the Quick Settings extension talks to the CLI; kast never calls
into a device from anywhere else.
.PP
This page is a command reference. For what each thing does and why, see
.I docs/USAGE.md
in the repository, or the web copy linked from the project's README.
.SH DISCOVERY
.TP
.BI targets " [--json] [--scan]"
Everything known: Chromecast, AirPlay and (after a scan) Miracast.
.B \-\-scan
issues fresh mDNS queries instead of reading the avahi cache.
.TP
.BI cast\-targets " [--json] [--scan]"
Chromecast only.
.TP
.BI airplay\-targets " [--json] [--scan]"
AirPlay only.
.TP
.BI miracast\-targets " [--json]"
Miracast, from an on\-demand Wi\-Fi P2P find (never cached).
.SH CASTING
.TP
.BI pick " [--miracast]"
The graphical "cast to\&..." picker, same as
.BR Super+K .
.B \-\-miracast
includes a Miracast scan.
.TP
.BI connect " target " "[url\-or\-file]"
Mirror this screen to
.IR target ,
or play a URL or file on it instead of mirroring.
.TP
.BI cast\-file " target " url\-or\-file
Play a file or URL on
.I target
without mirroring the screen.
.TP
.BI display\-connect " target"
Display mirroring specifically.
.TP
.B disconnect
Stop the active display stream.
.TP
.BI airplay\-pick " target"
.BR airplay\-cast (1)'s
GUI form: pick a video file, then cast it. Used by the tile.
.TP
.BI cast\-file\-pick " target"
Like
.I airplay\-pick
but for any target, AirPlay or Chromecast.
.TP
.BI airplay\-pair " target " "[--gui]"
One\-off pairing with an AirPlay TV, prompted in the terminal or, with
.BR \-\-gui ,
graphically.
.SH CONTROL
.TP
.B control
List controllable devices.
.TP
.BI control " target " caps
What this device actually supports.
.TP
.BI control " target " now\-playing
.TP
.BI control " target " action " [arg]"
Actions:
.BR stop ", " play ", " pause ", " play_pause ", " next ", " previous ,
.BI seek " seconds" ,
.BR volume_up ", " volume_down ,
.BI set_volume " 0\-100" ,
.BR power_on ", " power_off ,
.BI key " up|down|left|right|select|menu|home" ,
.BI launch_app " id" .
.TP
.BI control\-center " [target]"
The graphical remote window.
.SH RECEIVING
Three receivers, all off by default, all LAN\-facing. Each has the same six
verbs; substitute
.I audio\-receiver\-
or
.I youtube\-receiver\-
for
.I receiver\-
to reach the other two.
.TP
.BR receiver\-start ", " receiver\-stop ", " receiver\-restart ", " receiver\-status
AirPlay screen mirroring in, via
.BR uxplay (1).
.TP
.B toggle\-receiver
.TP
.B receiver\-run
Run in the foreground, for debugging.
.PP
The AirPlay screen receiver is PIN\-gated by default. Treat the 4\-digit PIN
as a speed bump, not authentication; stopping the receiver when idle is the
real control.
.SH AUDIO ROUTING
.TP
.BI sinks " [--json]"
Available PipeWire sinks.
.TP
.BI select\-sink " id|name"
.TP
.BI select\-airplay " [name]"
Route audio to an AirPlay speaker over PipeWire RAOP.
.TP
.B select\-local
Route audio back to this machine.
.TP
.B open\-sound
Open GNOME's Sound settings.
.SH DISPLAY BEHAVIOUR
.TP
.BI set\-mode " mirror|video\-overlay"
.TP
.B get\-mode
.TP
.B open\-display
GNOME Display settings.
.TP
.BI open\-display\-cast " [--drop\-wifi]"
The one\-click
.BR gnome\-network\-displays (1)
connect path.
.B \-\-drop\-wifi
releases the Wi\-Fi radio for a Miracast group on adapters that need it.
.TP
.B open\-display\-cast\-plain
Opens the
.B gnome\-network\-displays
GUI directly, skipping the one\-click D\-Bus path. The fallback on a GNOME
Shell older than that daemon needs.
.TP
.B reconnect\-wifi
Bring Wi\-Fi back after a Miracast session that dropped it.
.SH HEALTH AND UPDATES
.TP
.BI status " [--json]"
What's casting, what's receiving, what's discovered.
.TP
.B doctor
Full health check (tools, discovery, receivers, casting, audio routing,
desktop integration), with a fix hint per problem. Run this first when
anything misbehaves.
.TP
.B repair
Reinstall the pipx\-isolated
.I pyatv
and
.I catt
environments, for when an OS or Python upgrade leaves them pointing at a
Python that's gone.
.TP
.B version
.TP
.BI check\-update " [--json]"
Report only: is a newer release available.
.TP
.BI update " [--check [--json]] [--apt]"
Install the latest release in place.
.B \-\-check
reports without installing (same as
.BR check\-update ).
.B \-\-apt
also refreshes system packages; by default
.B update
leaves apt alone and needs no
.BR sudo .
A
.B .deb
install updates with the next
.B .deb
instead, and this verb refuses to touch it.
.TP
.BI install\-shortcut " [binding]"
Bind or rebind the cast\-picker keyboard shortcut. Default
.BR Super+K .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/kast/uxplay.conf
The receiver's config, sourced like a shell rc file. The preferences dialog
writes it; anything else editing it should treat it as code.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/kast/status.json
The read seam the Quick Settings tile watches instead of shelling out on
every open. Mode 0640, written atomically. Absent is a valid state, not a
failure.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B KAST_SHORTCUT
Overrides the default keybinding at install time (see
.BR install.sh ).
.TP
.B KAST_NO_UNSTABLE
Set to
.B 1
to refuse the unreviewed main\-branch install fallback when no release
asset exists.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Non\-zero on misuse or a failed action; the message on stderr says why.
.B doctor
and
.B kast\-healthcheck (1)
use exit status specifically to mean healthy/unhealthy, not just
success/failure of the invocation itself.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kast\-healthcheck (1),
.BR kast\-update (1),
.BR uxplay (1),
.BR gnome\-network\-displays (1)
.br
.I docs/USAGE.md
and
.I docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
in the kast repository.
.SH AUTHOR
asuramaya and kast contributors.
